  "review": {
    "notes": "audits/C132_ARENAS_20261001/dunesea-r2/visual-notes.d29.json",
    "findings": [
      "The new MID removes the predecessor mauve mountain/dune strip and cactus silhouettes from the battle runway. The accepted FAR is reused byte-for-byte.",
      "The new MID is a flat warm ochre sand runway; its top edge at approximately y=0.72 is brighter than the FAR ground and reads as a straight horizontal color/scale change.",
      "The selected second NEAR takes the new MID as its edit target and matches sand hue better than the first retained attempt. A horizontal grain/focus seam remains near y=0.88.",
      "New MID and NEAR omit thin plants, avoiding their old plant fringe problem, but the retained FAR still contains its original distant vegetation. No claim that every fringe is repaired.",
      "The full-size plates and composition were inspected. This is a cleaner but still visibly banded candidate, held for independent scoring and Dakk acceptance; no native battle or phone qualification."
    ],
    "scope": "Full-size image inspection only; no native film, player occlusion, acceptance or device qualification."
  },
